[# docs-src/repos/cx.cxd — the front door's page, repo-cx.html (RULED:
   DOCS-41, DOCS-47, DOCS-49 wave 2). The prose is ours; every fact on the
   page — what it pins, what builds on it, its links — is projected from
   registry/repos.cxd, deps.cxd and registry/modules.cxd when the guide is
   built (scripts/gen_site/repo_page.cx). One runnable example, from the
   front door's own corpus (conformance/llm/), replayed byte-exact. #]

[repo name=cx
  [intro
    """**TL;DR — we keep one front door.** `cx` is the tree that pins every
       repository of CX at a sha, builds the four builds of one binary from
       those pins, and serves this site. You install from it, you read from
       it, and every change to CX arrives through it: a pin moves only when
       the newer set is green together."""]
  [body
    """A pin is a sha, never a branch, and `deps.cxd` is the one place a pin
       is written: `make deps-sync` fetches each pinned repository into
       `deps/` and refuses a stale pin or a drifted checkout out loud
       rather than warning. The status table below is that document read
       back — what the front door builds on is the whole pin list, and the
       figure's left column draws it."""]
  [body
    """From those pins we build the four builds of `cx` — `data`, `embed`,
       `cli` and `platform` — the same binary name with a build-decided
       surface, so you take on only as much of CX as you need
       ([[rings]] is the map; the downloads page lists the four). The
       release, the installer this site's one-liner fetches, the guide and
       the primer are built here too, from the pinned corpora, so an example
       on any page of this site was replayed against the binary the same
       tree produced."""]
  [gives
    """No module of the language lives in the front door: every bundled
       module is pinned in from the repository that owns it, which is why the
       table below is empty and the plug-in figure's left column is long. What
       the front door gives you is the assembled binary, the site, the release
       and the installer — and one contract, that flags bind before the
       file."""]
  [try
    """The run surface is `cx [flags] FILE [args…]`: everything before the
       file is ours, everything after it belongs to the program. The case
       below is the corpus's own statement of that rule — the grant before
       the file, and the program reading what it was granted."""]
  [fixture id=ap-flags-after-file-right]
  [status
    """The front door is not pinned by anyone — it is the root that pins the
       rest. Its repository is public; the pins it names are private until the
       release cut."""]]
